{"step_index":253,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-08T09:57:26Z","content":"Here are the step-by-step instructions to run the **SecureChain** platform:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Run Locally via Terminals (Recommended for Development)\n\n#### Step 1: Start the Backend API (FastAPI)\nOpen your terminal/PowerShell window in the project folder and run:\n```powershell\ncd backend\npython main.py\n```\n* **Backend API Host**: [http://127.0.0.1:8001](http://127.0.0.1:8001)\n* **Interactive Swagger Documentation**: [http://127.0.0.1:8001/docs](http://127.0.0.1:8001/docs)\n\n#### Step 2: Start the Frontend UI (React + Vite)\nOpen a **second** terminal/PowerShell window and run:\n```powershell\ncd frontend\nnpm run dev\n```\n* **Web Security Dashboard**: [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173)\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Run via Docker Compose\n\nIf you have Docker Desktop installed, you can start both backend and frontend containers with a single command:\n\n```powershell\ndocker-compose up --build\n```\n* **Web UI**: [http://localhost:5173](http://localhost:5173)\n* **Backend API**: [http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000)\n\n---\n\n### Option 3: Deploy to Kubernetes / Minikube (Phase 13 Deliverable)\n\nTo deploy the application to a local Minikube or Kubernetes cluster:\n\n```powershell\n# 1. Apply Namespace and Secrets\nkubectl apply -f k8s/namespace.yaml\nkubectl apply -f k8s/secrets.yaml\n\n# 2. Deploy Backend & Frontend Deployments & Services\nkubectl apply -f k8s/backend-deployment.yaml\nkubectl apply -f k8s/backend-service.yaml\nkubectl apply -f k8s/frontend-deployment.yaml\nkubectl apply -f k8s/frontend-service.yaml\n\n# 3. Check Running Pod Status in Isolated Namespace\nkubectl get pods -n securechain-prod\n```"}
